{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"submission-close.json\", \"summary\": \"Turn 6 closed the active Candidate with the sourced protective mechanism and updated the map; every requirement, premise and prior result was preserved.\\n\\nMechanism that answers the suspicion. updateAttributes starts from the deps vector carried by the message, skips the row of the instance owner named in that message, and only raises components from local conflict knowledge, so a pre-accepting peer's reply vector dominates the leader's transmitted vector. mergeAttributes raises every component except the leader's own row, so with exactly one counted peer (N = 3, Thrifty, FastQuorumSize-1 = 1) the committed merged vector equals that peer's record in every compared component. For an owner-led instance the peer skips exactly the row mergeAttributes ignores, so leader and peer records coincide at the same vbal, the fast-commit branch installs the same vector locally, both fast-quorum members hold the committed vector, and any recovery quorum the recoverer can assemble (its own reply plus one of the other two replicas, both fast-quorum members) contains a holder. The source comment that equality need not be checked for N <= 3 with Thrifty therefore has a concrete mechanism, and the Candidate is recorded as explained by that mechanism rather than as a violated obligation.\\n\\nResidual, kept separate. The exposure is confined to one component and one context: a recovery-led phase 1 (LeaderId != owner), where mergeAttributes keeps the leader's own row value while the peer may hold a higher value for that row, so the peer's record can differ from the committed vector in that component; this needs the peer to know more about the leader's own row than the leader does, which no read path establishes for a live leader (a restart could, since Durable is false and no stable-store reader exists). That residual and the still-open accept-status question are carried in feedback as separate premises.\\n\\nMap updates (accepted base version 3). B4's unknown is replaced by the sourced conditional relationship, and core_overview's N<=3 open detail now records the mechanism and the confined residual, with map_changes entries for both objects and preserves explanations for unchanged requirements, dependencies and observation scope. One constraint worth noting for the next product: the validator rejects reinterpreting a Candidate's stored proposition, so the accepted question text was retained verbatim and the correction lives in feedback, question_updates and the map rather than in a rewritten question.\"}"}}
